I am now in the pants section.
I look at the clothes there.
I see a cotton pants there.
It is a bright red pants.
I take it to the fitting room.
I put on those pants.
This is a wide pants.
This is a very light pants.
It is very good for this heat.
I come out of the fitting room.
I ask the saleswoman the price.
"What is the price of these pants?" I ask.
"It is eight hundred rupees," she says.
I like those pants very much.
Its red colour is very beautiful.
"I am taking this," I tell her.
I take those red pants in my hands.
I need such cotton clothes for the heat in Kochi.
